        "description": "The web chat's message routes, run by the engine for the page's account (workshop-routes): the request's { path, method, query, body } in, { status, body } out. GET /messages and /messages/threads answer the person's conversations newest first ({conversations, next_before}); GET /messages/thread answers one conversation's messages (app and conversation_id). POST /messages/send keeps the person's words to one AI (app, conversation_id, text, client_id?) and POST /messages/send-all keeps them once in the shared Trillion conversation, each as one `message` row in the person's own records, written through the records door only, conditional on what was read. The same client_id sent again is the message already kept. A run reaches no AI's event inbox, so the answer says the message is kept and the AI reads it on its next connection; it never says delivered.",
